--
--
An x86 mfence (full memory barrier) written as inline assembly is recognised as
a barrier and orders the two register writes, so the ordering assertion holds.
Barriers are recognised by mnemonic across architectures (ARM dmb/dsb, Power
sync/lwsync, x86 mfence/sfence), so this is independent of --arch.
